## 2. Tech stack (detail)

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Hosting | Firebase Hosting (`ghostshopza.web.app`, `ghostshopza.firebaseapp.com`) |
| Database | Firestore (`africa-south1`) |
| Auth | Firebase Auth — Phone Number sign-in with reCAPTCHA |
| Functions | Firebase Cloud Functions v2 (Node.js) |
| Storage | Firebase Storage (`ghostshopza.firebasestorage.app`) |
| Push | Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) with VAPID key |
| Payments | Yoco (card checkout via hosted redirect, plus webhook) |
| Maps | Google Maps JavaScript API + Places API |
| Fonts | Inter (Google Fonts) |
| Icons | Font Awesome 6.0.0-beta3 (CDN) |
| PWA | Manifest + two service workers (`sw.js`, `firebase-messaging-sw.js`) |
| Build | **None.** ES modules loaded directly from `<script type="module">`. |

### Why no bundler

Deliberate choice to avoid build complexity. The project owner is not a professional developer and works primarily with AI assistants, so keeping the source → deploy path simple (edit file → Firebase serves it) is more valuable than tree-shaking. This may change later but is not a current priority.

