### 23.3 Notification data contract (IMPORTANT — confirmed this session)

Your admin writes notification docs with these exact field names:

```js
notifications/{id} {
  title:          string,
  message:        string,
  imageUrl:       string,        // optional, '' when absent
  icon:           string,        // e.g. 'fa-bell'
  recipientIds:   [string],      // array of user UIDs (empty = all)
  recipientNames: [string],      // for admin display
  recipients:     [string],      // same as recipientIds
  readBy:         [string],      // UIDs who've read
  deletedFor:     [string],      // UIDs who've deleted
  sentAt:         Timestamp,     // ← the customer modal queries by THIS
  sentBy:         string,        // admin UID or 'admin'
  recipientCount: number         // sent count, updated after push
}

The customer modal (in notifications.js) filters docs where:

recipientIds.length === 0 && recipients.length === 0 → broadcast to all

OR recipientIds.includes(user.uid) → targeted

OR recipients.includes(user.uid) → targeted (older docs)

And it hides docs where deletedFor.includes(user.uid).

