### 24.1 What was done in this session

**CSP (Content Security Policy) — final fixes**
- `firebase.json` CSP header expanded to allow the domains the app actually uses:
  - `https://www.gstatic.com` (Firebase JS SDK)
  - `https://apis.google.com` (Firebase Auth helper)
  - `https://www.google.com` (reCAPTCHA for phone sign-in)
  - `https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com` (Font Awesome CSS + fonts + SW fetch)
  - `https://*.cloudfunctions.net`, `https://*.run.app` (Cloud Functions calls)
  - `https://*.yoco.com` (Yoco checkout iframe)
- The CSP is now quite permissive (`'unsafe-inline'` on script-src and
  style-src, wildcard domains). Tightening is §16 issue #10 — future work.

**Service worker (`public/sw.js`) — rewritten**
- **Old SW was the cause of the store page hanging.** It intercepted every
  request (including external requests to Firebase, Google, cdnjs, Yoco) and
  cached them. When CSP blocked those external fetches, the SW returned fake
  `503 Offline` responses, which caused images to fall back to `placeholder.jpg`
  and broke the PWA install prompt.
- New SW policy:
  - Precaches only shell assets (HTML, base CSS, key JS, logo, manifest)
  - Network-first for HTML navigations
  - Cache-first only for **own-origin** static assets (`css/`, `js/`, `img/`,
    `config/`, `modals/`, `fonts/`)
  - **Pass-through for everything else** — the SW refuses to touch any
    request whose origin doesn't match `self.location.origin`
  - Cache name bumped to `ghost-shopper-v3` (forces purge of old caches)
  - Kill-switch message handler responds to `UNREGISTER` and `CLEAR_CACHES`

**Store page performance — root cause found and fixed**
- Owner reported store page hanging on first load. PWA install worked (cached)
  but fresh visits hung forever. Console showed `store.js booting...` then nothing.
- **Root cause:** top-level `await import('./analytics.js')` in `store.js` was
  blocking module evaluation. On the deployed site, `analytics.js` and its
  transitive Firebase SDK imports from `gstatic.com` were slow enough that the
  await never resolved. The loader never hid. The page never rendered.
- **Fix:** replaced with fire-and-forget `import('./analytics.js').then(...)`
  pattern. `store.js` now finishes evaluating immediately; analytics loads in
  the background and silently no-ops until ready.

