### 26.2 A1 verified — Yoco webhook confirmed working in production

**This is the most important outcome of these sessions.**

For weeks, the payment flow had one unverified assumption — "A1":

> **A1:** The `id` field returned by `POST /payments.yoco.com/api/checkouts`
> is equal to `webhook.payload.metadata.checkoutId` in the `payment.succeeded`
> event.

This was tested end-to-end on the live project on **9 October 2026** with
a real R2 test payment:

1. Owner added a real card to a test order.
2. `createCardOrder` ran, created a `pendingOrders` doc, called Yoco,
   stored the returned `checkoutId` (a `ch_...` string) on the pending doc.
3. Yoco processed the payment. The customer was redirected back to
   `order-confirmation.html`.
4. Yoco sent the `payment.succeeded` webhook to
   `https://us-central1-ghostshopza.cloudfunctions.net/yocoWebhook`.
5. Signature verification passed.
6. **The webhook matched `payload.metadata.checkoutId` to the stored
   `pendingOrders.checkoutId` on the first attempt.**
7. The conversion transaction ran and created a real `orders/{id}` doc.
8. The webhook log line was:
yocoWebhook: order 3zziUSjWLFFnojlVOVBH finalised (already=false)

text

**Conclusion: A1 is confirmed true in production.** `payload.metadata.checkoutId`
does contain the same checkout ID that `POST /checkouts` returned.

This means **card payments work end-to-end** on the live site. The order
