26.9 DO NOT CHANGE (additions to §0 and §26)
Add these to the DO NOT CHANGE list:

Do NOT revert checkout.js to client-side createYocoCheckout.
All order creation is server-side. Reverting re-opens the price-tamper
vulnerability.

Do NOT remove the signature verification from yocoWebhook.
Every webhook is HMAC-verified before any state changes.

Do NOT change the whsec_ secret handling. The secret is stored
as whsec_<base64> in Secret Manager, prefix stripped and
base64-decoded before use as the HMAC key.

Do NOT remove the idempotency transaction from createCardOrder.
The idempotencyKeys/{key} collection prevents duplicate orders and
duplicate Yoco checkouts on network retries.

Do NOT remove the pendingOrders transaction guard in the
webhook. Duplicate webhook deliveries cannot create duplicate
orders or double-consume wallet reservations.

Do NOT add a fallback path to yocoWebhook that matches on
payload.id. payload.id is the event ID, not a checkout ID.
Only payload.metadata.checkoutId, payload.metadata.pendingOrderId,
and (with cross-verification) payload.checkoutId are valid match
keys.

